ther_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cleippi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-25T15:25:36Z","updated_at":"2016-07-26T14:55:35Z","body":"For anyone winding up here looking for a good workaround for their API, I included this in my configuration file and it works just fine\n\n```\n        'response' => [\n            'formatters' => [\n                \\yii\\web\\Response::FORMAT_JSON => [\n                    'class' => 'yii\\web\\JsonResponseFormatter',\n                    'encodeOptions' => JSON_FORCE_OBJECT,\n                ],\n            ],\n        ],\n```\n\nEDIT: So this caused some unexpected problems. Most notably, my API went from outputting objects in this format\n\n```\n[\n    {\n        data here\n    },\n    ... more objects\n]\n```\n\nto outputting it in this format\n\n```\n{\n    0: {\n        data here\n    },\n    ... more objects\n}\n```\n\nSo when you force objects, it means _everything_. I'd still like there to be a better solution for Yii2 if possible, because I'm having trouble finding a good work around.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/234987095/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cleippi","id":13521443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTIxNDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13521443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.